interiors:
  GIBBS:
    caption: Nothing gets sealed, shed or signed for in this plant until the ledger it comes out of closes.
    standLine: Carbon in against carbon accounted for, and a magnet holding the sheet down.
    station:
      kind: panel
      title: Plant summary
      rows:
      # NOT "18 percent behind". v7: "Do not state the 18% shortfall separately;
      # the 82% Flight-Ready Methane bar communicates it." The bar is on screen
      # from the moment the opening card clears, so the row said the same thing
      # a second time and in a second unit.
      - { label: Methane against schedule, value: below target, status: alarm }
      - { label: Carbon accounted for, value: 99.8 of 100.0 kmol, status: normal }
      - { label: Power margin tonight, value: 18 kWh, status: low }
      # SHIFTS, not sols. The day noun is Shift throughout this campaign.
      - { label: Shifts to the window, value: '15', status: normal }
  EQUIL:
    caption: There is an amount of methane this mixture will settle at, and no amount of urgency moves it.
    standLine: The loop, the recycle line, and the heat nobody has counted yet.
    station:
      kind: panel
      title: Reactor loop
      rows:
      - { label: Loop pressure, value: 12.0 bar, status: normal }
      - { label: Bed inlet temperature, value: 612 K, status: alarm }
      - { label: Outlet average, value: 569 K, status: normal }
      - { label: Conversion this pass, value: 55 percent, status: low }
  KINET:
    caption: The bed is the only part of this plant that does something nothing else here can do.
    standLine: Nine sols of profiles, and an inlet running 24 kelvin hotter than a clean charge.
    station:
      kind: panel
      title: Catalyst bed
      rows:
      - { label: Inlet temperature, value: 612 K, status: alarm }
      - { label: Halide at the inlet, value: present and heavy, status: alarm }
      - { label: Surface area against fresh, value: within 3 percent, status: normal }
      - { label: Spare charges on the planet, value: '1', status: low }
  PHASE:
    caption: Anything that is not methane goes into the cold line as a liquid and stays there.
    standLine: 283 kelvin to 115 in one run of pipe, and a drier that has stopped holding.
    station:
      kind: panel
      title: Cold end
      rows:
      - { label: Drier differential pressure, value: high and rising, status: alarm }
      - { label: Condensate returned, value: 320 of 400 kmol, status: low }
      - { label: Radiator capacity, value: 78 percent of rated, status: alarm }
      - { label: Cold line outlet, value: 115 K, status: normal }
  SOIL:
    caption: Every number that leaves this room is measured against something sealed, or it does not leave.
    standLine: Two bottles, one alarm label, and a chloride figure nobody has checked.
    station:
      kind: panel
      title: Water plant
      rows:
      - { label: Wall chloride meter, value: 41 mg/L, status: alarm }
      - { label: Portable instrument, value: 12 mg/L, status: normal }
      - { label: Field blank from the cut, value: under 2 mg/L, status: normal }
      - { label: Polishing column duty, value: 71 percent spent, status: high }
  ELEC:
    caption: Splitting water is not something water does on its own, and the bill for that is electrical.
    standLine: Cells in series, and a store that starts every shift short of what the schedule assumed.
    station:
      kind: panel
      title: Electrolysis hall
      rows:
      - { label: Stack current, value: 10000 A, status: normal }
      - { label: Current efficiency, value: 92.0 percent, status: normal }
      - { label: Hydrogen in the store, value: 50 kmol, status: low }
      - { label: Water returned to the stack, value: 400 of 480 kmol, status: alarm }

